{"id":349788,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2299","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“ ‘The excellent lord of kings, Śuddhodana,","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3490,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349789,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2300","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“ ‘Similarly, Prince Mahādeva","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3494,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349790,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2301","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"This is usually taken to refer to the first five pupils of Śākyamuni, but Toh 555 specifies that two of them are Maudgalyāyana and Śāriputra, the Buddha’s two principal followers.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3497,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2300"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349791,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2302","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“ ‘Then King Mahāratha and the queen, wailing pitifully many times, removed their jewelry and, together with a great gathering of people, made offerings to the bones of their son. The bones of Mahāsattva they placed in this area, and they constructed this stūpa of seven precious materials.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3498,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349792,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2303","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“ ‘This Mahāsattva, having given his body to the tigress, prayed, “Through this gift of my body, may I afterward, in a future time, after countless eons have passed, accomplish the deeds of a buddha for beings.” ’","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3499,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349793,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2304","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“When this teaching was given, countless, innumerable beings, including humans and devas, developed the aspiration to attain the highest, most complete enlightenment.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3500,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349794,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2305","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“This was the cause and condition for the appearance of that stūpa. Then, through the blessing of the Buddha, the stūpa went back down into the ground.”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3501,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349795,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2306","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Chapter 27: Praise by All Bodhisattvas","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_heading","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3502,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349796,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2308","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Then those hundreds of thousands of bodhisattvas went to where the Tathāgata Suvarṇa­ratnākaracchatra­kūṭa was. When they arrived, they bowed down their heads to the feet of the Bhagavat Tathāgata Suvarṇa­ratnākaracchatra­kūṭa and arranged themselves to one side. Having arranged themselves to one side, those hundreds of thousands of bodhisattvas placed their palms together and praised the Tathāgata Suvarṇa­ratnākaracchatra­kūṭa with these verses:","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3503,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349797,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2309","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“The color of the Jina’s body is like refined gold;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3504,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349798,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2310","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“Your body is adorned by the excellent signs;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3508,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349799,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2311","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You have Brahmā’s voice, the beautiful voice of Brahmā.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3512,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349800,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2312","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You have completely stainless, immaculate, beautiful, bright light.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3516,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349801,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2313","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You have the supreme compassion for benefiting beings.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3520,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349802,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2314","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You bestow the bliss of deathlessness;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3524,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349803,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2315","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Only the first line of this verse is included in the Sanskrit.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3524,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2314"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349804,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2316","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"According to the Yongle, Lithang, Kangxi, and Choné rgyal ba. The Degé has rgyal ba’i.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3525,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2314"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349805,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2317","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"According to the Sanskrit. Although amṛta in the first line was translated as “deathlessness,” it appears that in the second line it was translated as amṛta (bdud rtsi), which is “the nectar of deathlessness.”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3525,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2314"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349806,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2318","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You are a jina who frees beings from suffering;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3528,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
