{"id":349811,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2324","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Then the bodhisattva Ruciraketu rose from his seat, and, with his upper robe over one shoulder, knelt on his right knee with palms together, bowed toward the Bhagavat, and then praised the Bhagavat with these verses:","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3545,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349812,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2325","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“Lord of munis, you have the signs of a hundred merits;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3546,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349813,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2326","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"From the Sanskrit udāra, which the Tibetan has translated as rgya che (“vast”).","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3548,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2325"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349814,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2327","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You pervade with light by radiating numerous light rays","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3550,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349815,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2328","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"According to the Sanskrit akula and the Yongle, Lithang, Kangxi, and Choné versions of Toh 556, which have gang ba. The Degé version has dang ba (“clear”).","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3551,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2327"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349816,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2329","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"According to the Tibetan and Nobel’s Sanskrit. The Bhagji edition has ratna (“jewel”).","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3551,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2327"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349817,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2330","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“They reach the vajra mountain, lord of mountains, Sumeru,","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3554,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349818,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2331","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You have a bright color and sense organs that are beautiful to behold.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3558,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349819,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2332","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You are adorned by the qualities of completely pure compassion.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3562,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349820,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2333","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You bring complete satisfaction and bring benefit;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3566,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349821,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2334","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“You are beautified by light rays that are like firelight;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3570,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349822,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2335","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“Your face is made beautiful by the rows of your teeth","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3574,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349823,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2336","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“A hair like white beryl curls to the right,","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3578,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349824,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2337","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"The Sanskrit and Tibetan have only “beryl,” but from context this appears to be “white beryl.” Toh 555 makes it clear that this is the ūrṇā hair between the Buddha’s eyebrows.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3578,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2336"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349825,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2338","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Chapter 29: The Conclusion","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_heading","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3582,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349826,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2340","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Then the noble goddess Bodhisattvasamuccayā praised the Bhagavat with these verses:","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3583,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349827,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2341","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“I pay homage to the Buddha who has pure knowledge,","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3584,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349828,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2342","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“Oh! Oh! The Buddha’s magnificence is infinite!","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3588,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349829,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2343","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“In order that he may care for all beings,","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3592,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349830,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2344","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“The Tathāgata Śākyamuni is the lord of peace;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3596,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349831,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2345","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“In that way, the bodies of the disciples are empty;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3600,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349832,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2346","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“I always, constantly think of the Buddha;","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3604,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349833,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2347","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“I constantly kneel in one narrow spot,","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3608,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349834,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2348","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“I am completely burned by the fire of my grief.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3612,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349835,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2349","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"The Sanskrit translates as “beings are in extreme thirst.”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3614,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2348"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349836,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2350","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"According to the Sanskrit prahladyet and Toh 557, which has sim. Toh 556 has tshim (“satisfy”).","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3615,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2348"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349837,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2351","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“I pray that you, the Guide, will be compassionate to me.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3616,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349838,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2352","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"“All beings have the nature of a dream.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3620,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349839,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2353","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"The Sanskrit has mahānta. The Tibetan translates as tshe dang ldan pa, the usual translation of āyuṣman.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3623,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2352"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349840,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2354","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"The Khotanese Sanskrit and Toh 555 have additional verses at this point.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3623,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2352"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349841,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2355","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"The Bhagavat then rose from his seat and with the voice of Brahmā said, “Noble goddess, well done! Well done!”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3624,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349842,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2356","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"When the Bhagavat had spoken, the noble goddess Bodhisattvasamuccayā, the noble goddess Sarasvatī, and all the other goddesses—the noble goddess Śrī and all the rest of the entire assembly of goddesses—and Vaiśravana and all the other kings of devas, and the assembly that had all the different kinds of disciples, and the world with its devas, humans, asuras, and gandharvas rejoiced and praised the words of the Bhagavat.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3625,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349843,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2357","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"The Sanskrit here translates as “great goddesses.”","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3625,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2356"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349844,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2359","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Colophon","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_heading","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3626,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349845,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2360","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"Translated and revised by the Paṇḍitas Jinamitra and Nelendrabodhi, and by the Lotsawa Yeshe Dé, the chief editor, and definitively revised according to the new language reform.","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_main","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3627,"relation_ids":["toh556"],"export_role":"primary"}
{"id":349846,"corpus":"84000-tei","language":"en","collection_name":"kangyur","work_id":"UT22084-089-013","segment_id":"UT22084-089-013-2361","title":"The Sūtra of the Sublime Golden Light (2)","raw_text":"This reform of the spelling of written Tibetan—which included, for example, eliminating the secondary suffix da—was made in 816, during the reign of King Ralpachen (born ca. 806, r. 815–38).","source_path":"84000/data-tei/translations/kangyur/translations/089-013_toh556-the_sutra_of_the_sublime_golden_light_2.xml","source_sha":"bdfc81c9aecdfaf93e084ab64a885577de773046","evidence_class":"authoritative_structured","text_role":"translation_note","witness":"toh556","sequence_no":3627,"relation_ids":["UT22084-089-013-2360"],"export_role":"primary"}
